# Multimodal Image-to-Text Pipeline for Mammography Analysis
**Master's Thesis Project — KTH Royal Institute of Technology & Stockholm University**

This repository contains the codebase for my Master's thesis investigating the transition from standard single-view object detection to multimodal Vision-Language Models (VLMs) for automated BI-RADS classification and mammography report generation.

## Project Architecture
The research is structured into three sequential phases to rigorously evaluate the necessity and performance of advanced spatial and linguistic modeling in dense breast tissue analysis.

### 📁 [Phase 1: Single-View Faster R-CNN Baseline](./Phase-1-Single-View-Baseline)
* **Objective:** Establish a performance baseline using a standard 2D object detector (Faster R-CNN with ResNet-50 FPN) on the VinDr-Mammo dataset.
* **Status:** ✅ Completed
* **Key Finding:** Quantified the high false-positive rate (FPPI) caused by overlapping tissue in single-view analysis, justifying the need for multi-view architectures.

### 📁 Phase 2: Cross-Attention Transformers (In Progress)
* **Objective:** Implement a multi-view architecture (e.g., RT-DETR) to enable spatial token exchange between Cranio-Caudal (CC) and Medio-Lateral Oblique (MLO) views.

### 📁 Phase 3: Vision-Language Model Fine-Tuning (Upcoming)
* **Objective:** Apply Parameter-Efficient Fine-Tuning (LoRA) to adapt an open-source VLM for generating descriptive clinical medical reports and BI-RADS classifications based on multi-view inputs.

## Dataset
This project utilizes the [VinDr-Mammo Dataset](https://physionet.org/content/vindr-mammo/1.0.0/), consisting of 20,000 full-field digital mammography (FFDM) images with radiologist-annotated bounding boxes and BI-RADS classifications.

